WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.860
A yeast mutant called sec1 grows at 25 degrees Celsius.

2
00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:15.020
At 37 degrees, it keeps making secretory enzymes, but they stay inside.

3
00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:20.920
The pool inside rises up to eightfold, packed into membrane-bound vesicles.

4
00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:24.440
These vesicles formed, so budding worked.

5
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:26.220
Something later failed.

6
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.610
A vesicle first needs a coat.

7
00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:36.530
At the ER, a small switch called Sar1 binds the membrane when it carries GTP.

8
00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:41.450
Sar1 brings in the Sec23/24 complex.

9
00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:44.550
That complex brings in the outer cage.

10
00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:47.030
Together they make COPII.

11
00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:51.530
The coat grabs the cargo and bends the membrane into a bud.

12
00:00:52.383 --> 00:00:56.103
Once it has budded, the vesicle needs an address.

13
00:00:56.983 --> 00:01:00.203
A Rab is a small switch anchored in a membrane.

14
00:01:01.083 --> 00:01:06.483
With GDP bound, it is held in the cytosol by a protein called GDI.

15
00:01:07.623 --> 00:01:14.543
A GEF on the right membrane loads GTP, and the Rab lights up like a sign over one

16
00:01:14.543 --> 00:01:19.923
loading bay. It recruits tethers, long proteins that capture the vesicle.

17
00:01:20.717 --> 00:01:26.137
Capture is not fusion, because two membranes resist merging.

18
00:01:27.277 --> 00:01:28.697
SNAREs supply the force.

19
00:01:29.897 --> 00:01:37.177
Four motifs, called Qa, Qb, Qc and R, wind into one bundle.

20
00:01:37.977 --> 00:01:43.537
The bundle zippers toward the membrane anchors and pulls the bilayers together until

21
00:01:43.537 --> 00:01:51.657
they fuse. Afterwards all four sit in one membrane, and NSF uses ATP to pull them

22
00:01:51.657 --> 00:01:52.757
apart for reuse.

23
00:01:53.717 --> 00:01:56.657
Test tubes show that these steps come apart.

24
00:01:57.717 --> 00:02:01.737
Vesicles made with GMP-PNP still formed.

25
00:02:02.717 --> 00:02:08.717
This GTP analogue cannot be hydrolyzed, and the vesicles kept their coat and failed

26
00:02:08.717 --> 00:02:09.977
to target and fuse.

27
00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:16.717
Once vesicles had docked, fusion no longer cared about GDI, a protein that pulls

28
00:02:16.717 --> 00:02:17.837
Rabs off membranes.

29
00:02:19.297 --> 00:02:24.317
Truncated HOPS tethers still tethered liposomes, but failed to promote fusion.

30
00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:33.170
Back to sec1. A vesicle needs a coat to bud, a Rab and a tether to be caught, and

31
00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:39.870
SNAREs to fuse. Those vesicles formed, so the coat worked, and a later step failed.

32
00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:42.690
Each step can fail alone.

33
00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:46.670
Budding, targeting and fusion are separate steps.
